{
    "background_story": "Zakai was a majestic Egyptian Plover (Pluvianus aegyptius), known for his striking black and white feathers. He lived in the scorching deserts of North Africa, where he had adapted to the harsh conditions. Zakai was a devoted mate and parent, taking turns with his partner to incubate their eggs and care for their young. One fateful day, a severe sandstorm rolled in, threatening to destroy their nest. Zakai shielded his family with his wings, protecting them from the blistering winds and stinging sand. When the storm passed, the nest was intact, and Zakai's family was safe. His selfless act earned him the respect and admiration of the other birds in the colony, who looked up to him as a symbol of devotion and bravery.",
